cookbook/
    The JOSE Cookbook (the examples of RFC 7520 as JSON files), https://github.com/ietf-jose/cookbook, files of the
    master branch downloaded from https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ietf-jose/cookbook/master/ on 2026-10-26:
    jwk/, jws/, jwe/, curve25519/ and 6.nesting_signatures_and_encryption.json.
    License: the Unlicense (cookbook/LICENSE).
    Not included: rfc7797/, whose examples do not follow RFC 7797 (no "crit" listing "b64", and a protected header
    whose base64url is not that of the header); RFC 7797 is tested with the examples of its text instead.
    Known errors kept as they are: the input of jwe/5_13 names its content encryption "A128CBC-H256" (its headers
    say "A128CBC-HS256"), and the ephemeral key of curve25519/ecdh-es.json in "encrypting_key" is not the one of
    its header (the file says it is not reproducible).
    Used: every key, every output of every example (verified or decrypted with the keys whose algorithms are
    implemented: RSA1_5 is not), and the deterministic steps (HMAC, RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5 and EdDSA signatures,
    content encryption, AES key wrapping, PBES2, AES-GCM key wrapping, ECDH-ES with the ephemeral key given).

json_web_signature_test.json, json_web_encryption_test.json
    Project Wycheproof, testvectors_v1/json_web_signature_test.json and json_web_encryption_test.json of
    https://github.com/C2SP/wycheproof, downloaded on 2026-10-26.
    License: Apache License 2.0.
    Used: every test, with the divergences that tests/protocol/jwt/jws.rs and jwe.rs list with their reasons
    (keys whose "alg" or "key_ops" the specifications do not let them use, files whose values are corrupted, a
    JSON serialization that this library reads, and RSA1_5).

